-- title:
--   Strict parent repairs split relative to one fixed winning row
-- statement:
--   Fix a zero-tolerance row p that accepts at target t_j and guard g_j in a labelled tournament. Assume g_j≤t_l and g_l≤t_j. Every single-bit flip making the zero-tolerance parent at t_l,g_l accept belongs either to an outgoing strict repair from p, to the downward-sensitivity sets at g_l of p’s target children, or to the set of repairs making row p itself accept at t_l,g_l.
